infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The interop seam runs both ways
  desc Each direction has its own contract, its own trap, and its own fix
  compares
    - label require(esm) — from CJS
      children
        - label Returns the namespace object
          desc default lives under .default, named exports as members
        - label Synchronous evaluation only
          desc Must finish without yielding to the event loop
        - label Top-level await throws
          desc ERR_REQUIRE_ASYNC_MODULE — the graph turned async
        - label Escape hatch: await import()
          desc Inside an async function it can wait for the loop
    - label import cjs — from ESM
      children
        - label module.exports becomes default
          desc import pkg from "dep" is module.exports itself
        - label Named exports via a static lexer
          desc cjs-module-lexer scans the source before it runs
        - label Dynamic exports are undefined
          desc Computed keys and Object.assign are invisible to it
        - label Fix: default-import then destructure
          desc import pkg from "dep"; const { foo } = pkg
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
